      "mergeID": "63e15de1c913e01466795115",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Description of the bug: The list of available instances per world will only load once per play session. Makes hopping publics very annoying cause after a while I could be hopping into a totally dead world thinking it has 20 people in it. I can also not see new instances created after I launch the game.\n\nI can see using the website that the instances update there so must be a client issue.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n- Browse world tab, open some worlds and load their instance list\n\n- Play the game for a bit\n\n- Open the same worlds in the big menu, instance list is unchanged/wont update for every world page I loaded earlier in the play session.\n\n- Only way to fetch new instance data for those worlds is to restart the game\n\nCheck images for reference, the black cat instance list doesn't update. Windows clock in the lower right of the images. The instance I'm in changes but nothing else. Between image 1 and 2 I've rejoined, visited other worlds, clicked around on other stuff in the big menu.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1277] World instance list only loads once per world per session",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "631ecd871744d244ce619e64",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
